        "comments": "Chromosome-level reassembly of the pearl millet Tift?23D2B1-P1-P5 inbred cultivar genotype. The fasta file contains both the chromosomes and the unplaced and unlocalised sequences of the assembly. Pearl millet is a cross-pollinated diploid with 7 chromosomes (2n = 14). Its genome size was previously estimated at 1.76?Gb with more than 80% repetitive sequences (Varshney et al. 2017). Oxford Nanopore long reads and optical mapping were used for the assembly. The pearl millet reference genome (GCA_002174835.1) was used as a guide for chromosomes building. In depth study, along with manual curation, were carried out to validate the orientation and position of the scaffolds, and opticals maps from another inbred genotype (ERZ14864807) were used as a control of the continuity of the assembly. Correction with Illumina shot reads (SRP063925) was also performed.",
